 faq=[('h3','[H2] Frequently Asked Questions'),
  ('p','**What is a fire escape hood?**'),
  ('p','A fire escape hood, also called a smoke hood or emergency escape hood, is a clear hood with filters that a person pulls over their head to breathe filtered air while escaping a fire. It is for escape only, not for fighting a fire or going back into a building.'),
  ('p','**How long does the iEvac protect?**'),
  ('p','ASTM E2952 requires at least 15 minutes of protection against each test gas. In that testing, the iEvac protected against carbon monoxide for more than 45 minutes at 3,000 ppm and against hydrogen cyanide for more than 90 minutes at 400 ppm.'),
  ('p','**Can the iEvac be used more than once?**'),
  ('p','No. It is for one-time use only. An unused hood has a shelf life of 5½ years from the date of manufacture.'),
  ('p','**Can people with glasses or beards wear it?**'),
  ('p','Yes. It comes in one universal size and can be worn with eyeglasses, beards, and long hair, and no fit test is needed.')],
